    <!-- Edibles Warning Box -->
    <div class="highlight-box highlight-gold" style="margin:2rem 0;">
      <h4 style="color:var(--accent-gold);margin-bottom:0.5rem;">⚠️ The Edibles Problem — Read This Carefully</h4>
      <p>
        Edibles are responsible for the majority of cannabis-related emergency department visits. The delay between
        consumption and effect (30-120 minutes) leads users to consume more, assuming the first dose "didn't work" —
        then both doses hit simultaneously. THC in edibles is converted by the liver to
        <strong>11-hydroxy-THC</strong>, which is more potent and crosses the blood-brain barrier more readily than
        inhaled THC. The result: an overwhelming experience that can last 8+ hours.
        <strong>The golden rule: start with 2.5-5mg THC, wait a full 2 hours, then decide about more.</strong>
        Even experienced smokers should start low with edibles.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Harm Reduction Tips -->
    <div class="harm-reduction-section">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;color:var(--text);">Harm Reduction Best Practices</h3>
      <div class="harm-grid">
        <div class="harm-tip harm-tip-green">
          <div class="harm-tip-icon">🐢</div>
          <h4>Start Low, Go Slow</h4>
          <p>Begin with the lowest effective dose — especially with edibles. You can always take more; you cannot take less. This is the single most important harm reduction practice.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="harm-tip harm-tip-green">
          <div class="harm-tip-icon">⚖️</div>
          <h4>Choose Balanced Products</h4>
          <p>Select products with a ratio of THC to CBD rather than pure THC. CBD modulates some of THC's anxiety-producing effects. Ratios of 1:1 or 2:1 (THC:CBD) are generally better tolerated.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="harm-tip harm-tip-yellow">
          <div class="harm-tip-icon">🏷️</div>
          <h4>Know Your Source</h4>
          <p>Use lab-tested, licensed dispensary products with verified cannabinoid content. Unregulated products may contain pesticides, mold, heavy metals, or inaccurate labeling — all serious health hazards.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="harm-tip harm-tip-yellow">
          <div class="harm-tip-icon">🚗</div>
          <h4>Never Drive Impaired</h4>
          <p>Cannabis impairs driving regardless of tolerance. Plan transportation before consuming. Effects from edibles may last 6-8 hours — plan accordingly.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="harm-tip harm-tip-red">
          <div class="harm-tip-icon">🧪</div>
          <h4>Avoid Dangerous Combinations</h4>
          <p>Cannabis combined with alcohol dramatically increases impairment and adverse effects. Avoid mixing with other sedatives, stimulants, or opioids. Know your medications' interactions with CBD.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="harm-tip harm-tip-red">
          <div class="harm-tip-icon">👶</div>
          <h4>Age &amp; Medical Exclusions</h4>
          <p>Avoid if under 21 (ideally 25+ for brain development). Never use during pregnancy or breastfeeding. Avoid if you have personal or family history of psychosis, schizophrenia, or bipolar disorder.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="harm-tip harm-tip-green">
          <div class="harm-tip-icon">🌍</div>
          <h4>Set &amp; Setting Matter</h4>
          <p>Your environment, mindset, and companions significantly influence the experience. First-time or low-tolerance users should consume in a safe, comfortable setting with a trusted, sober friend present.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="harm-tip harm-tip-yellow">
          <div class="harm-tip-icon">📉</div>
          <h4>Take Tolerance Breaks</h4>
          <p>Regular use builds tolerance and increases dependence risk. Periodic tolerance breaks (2-4 weeks) maintain sensitivity, reduce CUD risk, and can help assess your relationship with cannabis.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>


