<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 6 · DOSING GUIDE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="section-alt" id="dosing">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="eyebrow">Pharmacology</div>
      <h2>💊 Understanding Dosage</h2>
      <p>Dosing cannabis is highly individual. Body weight, metabolism, tolerance, endocannabinoid system sensitivity,
      consumption method, and genetics all influence response. Use these as starting frameworks, not fixed prescriptions.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="dosing-grid">

      <!-- THC Dosing -->
      <div class="dosing-column">
        <div class="dosing-header thc-dosing-header">
          <div class="dosing-molecule">Δ9-THC</div>
          <h3>THC Dosing Guide</h3>
          <p>Psychoactive — effects are strongly dose-dependent. Tolerance significantly increases dosage requirements over time.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="dose-level dose-micro">
          <div class="dose-level-header">
            <div class="dose-range">1–2.5 mg THC</div>
            <div class="dose-name">Microdose</div>
          </div>
          <div class="dose-bar-wrap"><div class="dose-bar" style="width:10%;"></div></div>
          <p>Subtle mood enhancement, mild creativity boost, slight pain relief. No perceptible psychoactive effect in most users. Ideal for first-timers, medical users needing function, daytime use, or those sensitive to THC. Popular in microdosing communities for productivity and mood.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="dose-level dose-low">
          <div class="dose-level-header">
            <div class="dose-range">2.5–10 mg THC</div>
            <div class="dose-name">Low Dose</div>
          </div>
          <div class="dose-bar-wrap"><div class="dose-bar" style="width:25%;"></div></div>
          <p>Moderate relief of pain, anxiety, and sleep difficulties. Mild psychoactive effect — euphoria, relaxation, altered perception. Standard recreational dose for occasional users. Most legal edible products in regulated markets default to 5mg or 10mg doses. Good starting point for medical applications.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="dose-level dose-moderate">
          <div class="dose-level-header">
            <div class="dose-range">10–30 mg THC</div>
            <div class="dose-name">Moderate Dose</div>
          </div>
          <div class="dose-bar-wrap"><div class="dose-bar" style="width:50%;"></div></div>
          <p>Stronger psychoactive effects — significant euphoria, perceptual changes, time distortion, increased appetite. More potent pain and sleep effects. Appropriate for experienced users with established tolerance. May cause anxiety or discomfort in those without tolerance. Used in clinical trials for chronic pain and sleep disorders.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="dose-level dose-high">
          <div class="dose-level-header">
            <div class="dose-range">30–50 mg THC</div>
            <div class="dose-name">High Dose</div>
          </div>
          <div class="dose-bar-wrap"><div class="dose-bar" style="width:72%;"></div></div>
          <p>Very strong effects — primarily for individuals with high tolerance or specific medical conditions (e.g., cancer pain, severe sleep disorders). Significant impairment likely. Increased risk of adverse effects (paranoia, anxiety, disorientation) even in experienced users. Not appropriate for occasional users.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="dose-level dose-veryhigh">
          <div class="dose-level-header">
            <div class="dose-range">50+ mg THC</div>
            <div class="dose-name">Very High / Clinical Range</div>
          </div>
          <div class="dose-bar-wrap"><div class="dose-bar" style="width:95%;"></div></div>
          <p>Extreme effects — primarily relevant in clinical settings or for patients with very high tolerance from chronic medical use. High risk of acute adverse reactions in most users. Cannabis cannot cause a fatal overdose (no lethal dose established in humans), but very high doses can produce extreme disorientation, anxiety, rapid heart rate, and temporary psychosis-like symptoms that, while not life-threatening, are highly distressing.</p>
          <div class="dose-warning">⚠️ Not for recreational use. Seek medical guidance.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- CBD Dosing -->
      <div class="dosing-column">
        <div class="dosing-header cbd-dosing-header">
          <div class="dosing-molecule">CBD</div>
          <h3>CBD Dosing Guide</h3>
          <p>Non-psychoactive — no "high" at any dose. Generally well-tolerated. Effects are subtle and build over consistent use for many conditions.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="dose-level dose-cbd-wellness">
          <div class="dose-level-header">
            <div class="dose-range">10–25 mg/day</div>
            <div class="dose-name">General Wellness</div>
          </div>
          <div class="dose-bar-wrap"><div class="dose-bar" style="width:15%;background:#2dd4bf;"></div></div>
          <p>Starting point for CBD supplementation for general wellbeing, mild stress relief, or sleep support. Effects are subtle — many users don't notice dramatic changes but report cumulative improvements over 2-4 weeks of consistent use. Works better with consistent daily dosing than occasional use.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="dose-level dose-cbd-anxiety">
          <div class="dose-level-header">
            <div class="dose-range">15–50 mg/day</div>
            <div class="dose-name">Anxiety &amp; Mood</div>
          </div>
          <div class="dose-bar-wrap"><div class="dose-bar" style="width:30%;background:#2dd4bf;"></div></div>
          <p>Range studied in human anxiety trials. The landmark 2011 social anxiety study used 600mg pre-dose (acute), while ongoing anxiety management typically uses lower daily doses. Most over-the-counter CBD products in this range show benefit for situational anxiety and stress. Interacts with 5-HT1A serotonin receptors — similar pathway to SSRIs, but not equivalent in effect strength.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="dose-level dose-cbd-pain">
          <div class="dose-level-header">
            <div class="dose-range">20–100 mg/day</div>
            <div class="dose-name">Pain &amp; Inflammation</div>
          </div>
          <div class="dose-bar-wrap"><div class="dose-bar" style="width:55%;background:#2dd4bf;"></div></div>
          <p>Higher doses required for meaningful pain modulation. CBD affects pain through multiple mechanisms: TRPV1 desensitization (pain receptor), ECS anandamide elevation, and anti-inflammatory COX-2 inhibition. Topical CBD products in this range are used for localized joint and muscle pain. Oral CBD for neuropathic pain typically requires the higher end of this range.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="dose-level dose-cbd-neuro">
          <div class="dose-level-header">
            <div class="dose-range">100–300 mg/day</div>
            <div class="dose-name">Neurological / Sleep Disorders</div>
          </div>
          <div class="dose-bar-wrap"><div class="dose-bar" style="width:80%;background:#2dd4bf;"></div></div>
          <p>Range used in MS, Parkinson's, and sleep disorder studies. At this level, potential drug interactions become more clinically relevant — particularly CYP enzyme inhibition affecting other medications. Physician guidance recommended. May cause drowsiness, dry mouth, or diarrhea at the higher end. Generally well-tolerated compared to pharmaceutical alternatives.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="dose-level dose-cbd-clinical">
          <div class="dose-level-header">
            <div class="dose-range">200–300+ mg/day</div>
            <div class="dose-name">Clinical Epilepsy (Medical Supervision Required)</div>
          </div>
          <div class="dose-bar-wrap"><div class="dose-bar" style="width:95%;background:#2dd4bf;"></div></div>
          <p>Range used in FDA-approved Epidiolex trials for treatment-resistant epilepsy. Starting dose of 5mg/kg/day, titrated to 20mg/kg/day maximum. Requires blood level monitoring for drug interactions (Epidiolex elevates clobazam levels significantly). Liver enzyme elevation possible at high doses — liver function monitoring recommended. This dose range is <strong>only appropriate under specialist neurological care</strong>.</p>
          <div class="dose-warning dose-warning-teal">⚕️ Medical supervision required at this dose range.</div>
        </div>

        <!-- CBD Side Effects -->
        <div class="cbd-effects-box">
          <h4 style="margin-bottom:1rem;color:#fff;">CBD: Common Side Effects &amp; Interactions</h4>
          <div class="grid-2" style="gap:1rem;">
            <div>
              <div style="color:var(--primary);font-weight:600;font-size:0.85rem;margin-bottom:0.5rem;">GENERALLY BENIGN:</div>
              <ul class="check-list">
                <li>Dry mouth</li>
                <li>Mild drowsiness (higher doses)</li>
                <li>Appetite changes</li>
                <li>Mild diarrhea (high doses)</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div style="color:#f87171;font-weight:600;font-size:0.85rem;margin-bottom:0.5rem;">WATCH FOR:</div>
              <ul class="cross-list">
                <li>Liver enzyme elevation (high doses)</li>
                <li>Drug interactions (CYP enzymes)</li>
                <li>Warfarin level changes</li>
                <li>Antiepileptic level changes</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- Final Disclaimer -->
    <div class="final-disclaimer">
      <div class="disclaimer-icon-large">⚕️</div>
      <div>
        <h3 style="color:var(--text);margin-bottom:0.75rem;">A Final Word on Medical Use</h3>
        <p>
          Cannabis medicine is a legitimate and rapidly evolving field, but it exists within a complex landscape of
          legal variation, incomplete research, and significant individual variability. The science is clear that
          cannabis offers real benefits for real conditions — and real risks that deserve respect. Effective medical
          use combines appropriate product selection, accurate dosing, awareness of personal risk factors, and
          ideally, involvement of a knowledgeable healthcare provider.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-top:0.75rem;">
          If you're considering cannabis for a medical condition: start by consulting your physician or a
          cannabis-informed pharmacist, document your symptoms before and during use, start with the lowest
          effective dose of a product with verified lab testing, and give it sufficient time — many therapeutic
          effects are cumulative and may take 2-4 weeks of consistent use to fully emerge.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

</Layout>

